          "final_text_tail": "All 830 tests pass. The implementation is complete and verified.\n\nThe implementation adds two validation methods to `InternationalizationExtension` in `src/jinja2/ext.py`:\n\n- **`_validate_trans_variables(variables, parser, lineno)`** \u2014 iterates all trans-block variables and checks each name is a valid Python identifier, isn't a reserved translation function name (reusing the existing `GETTEXT_FUNCTIONS` tuple: `_`, `gettext`, `ngettext`, `pgettext`, `npgettext`), then delegates to expression validation.\n- **`_validate_trans_expression(name, expr, parser, lineno)`** \u2014 inspects the AST node type, allowing `Const`, `Name`, `Call` (with a `Name` function), `Getattr`, `Filter`, and `Test`, while rejecting `TemplateData`, `Output`, and other complex nested expressions.\n\nThe validation is wired into `parse()` right after variable collection (the `for name in referenced:` loop) and before `_make_node()` is called, so it covers both explicitly declared and body-referenced variables, works with `{% pluralize %}`, and respects the `trimmed`/`notrimmed` handling. All failures use `parser.fail()` with `TemplateSyntaxError` and messages containing the required phrases (\"Invalid variable name\"/\"Python identifiers\", \"conflicts with translation function names\", \"template data\"/\"translation contexts\").",
