          "final_text_tail": "lias** `conditional_i18n = ConditionalI18nExtension`\n- **`parse()`** \u2014 parses the condition via `parser.parse_expression()`, then optional variables (commas as optional separators), `trimmed`/`notrimmed` modifiers, the singular block, optional `pluralize` block, and the **mandatory** `fallback` block. Registers free names as `Name` nodes and handles the `num`/`_trans` plural-expression logic mirroring the standard `trans` tag.\n- **`_parse_block()`** \u2014 parses content until one of the given end names (or `endctrans`), collecting referenced variable names and building the `%(name)s` format string. Raises \"unclosed conditional translation block\" on EOF.\n- **`_trim_whitespace()`** \u2014 same `_ws_re` regex as the standard `trans` tag.\n- **`_make_conditional_node()`** \u2014 builds an `If` node: true branch \u2192 `gettext`/`ngettext` call (new-style kwargs or old-style `Mod`, wrapped in `MarkSafeIfAutoescape`); false branch \u2192 fallback `TemplateData` with explicit `MarkSafeIfAutoescape` + `Mod` substitution (since fallback never goes through gettext).\n\n**Error handling verified:**\n- Missing `fallback` \u2192 `TemplateSyntaxError` containing \"expected 'fallback' block\"\n- Unclosed `ctrans` \u2192 `TemplateSyntaxError` \"unclosed conditional translation block\"\n- Duplicate variable \u2192 `TemplateAssertionError` \"...defined twice.\"\n\nAll 830 existing tests pass; behavior for variable substitution, percent-escaping, pluralization, `num` handling, autoescaping, and `newstyle_gettext` matches the standard `trans` tag.",
